teSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"uOWCj0MndWAxcicR","name":"Speak with Plants (Constant; Trees Only)","type":"spell","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/spells/speak-with-plants.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{"core":{}},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>You can ask questions of and receive answers from plants, but the spell doesn't make them more friendly or intelligent than normal. Most normal plants have a distinctive view of the world around them, so they don't recognize details about creatures or know anything about the world beyond their immediate vicinity. Cunning plant monsters are likely to be terse and evasive, while less intelligent ones often make inane comments.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"speak-with-plants","_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["concentrate","manipulate","plant"],"rarity":"common","traditions":["primal"]},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Core Rulebook","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"level":{"value":4},"requirements":"","target":{"value":""},"range":{"value":""},"area":null,"time":{"value":"2"},"duration":{"value":"10 minutes","sustained":false},"damage":{},"defense":null,"cost":{"value":""},"location":{"value":"wp2qOu1Xog4vFT1b","heightenedLevel":4},"counteraction":false},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.qvwIwJ9QBihy8R0t","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"kDSsuCtfl7LzVJiT","name":"Constant Spells","type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{"core":{}},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.ConstantSpells]</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"constant-spells","_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"category":"interaction","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""},"weapon":{"value":""}},"ownership":{"default":0,"ldigRFmLUDwvP1vo":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.kakyXBG5WA8c6Zfd","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}}],"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{"pf2e":{"lootable":false},"core":{}},"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":22,"temp":0,"max":22,"details":""},"ac":{"value":16,"details":"","base":16},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":25,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"emotion"}],"weaknesses":[{"type":"fire","value":3}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common","wildsong","fey"],"details":"speak with plants (trees only)"},"level":{"value":0},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Diminutive leshies are often the prized friends of druids, rangers, and other nature lovers. Not so with leshy husks, whose corruption has left them devoid of whatever charm and grace they may have once possessed. Their drooping branches, gray foliage, and cracked bark skin make leshy husks stand out noticeably from their unwarped kin. Nevertheless, leshy husks excel at ambush tactics, and they ably sneak through the blighted swamps, slashed-and-burned forests, and salted plains in which they typically dwell.</p>\n<p>As with all husks, leshy husks vary widely in their abilities depending on which type of leshy they sprouted from. The leshy husk presented here was once a tree leshy.</p>\n<h2>Leshy Husk Minions</h2>\n<p>Stronger husks, including dryad and arboreal husks, sometimes take along leshy husks as minions and servants. Most such \"husk masters\" are smarter or more ambitious than typical husks of their kind, and their goals often include domination of the local area or the ruination of a nearby settlement.</p>\n<h2>Husk</h2>\n<p>Plant creatures share a special bond with the natural world that few other beings can completely understand or appreciate. When the bond to its realm is broken or severed, a sentient plant creature's rage can transform it into a terrible shadow of its former self. Benign and even friendly plants like leshies, arboreals, and dryads all run the risk of this horrible metamorphosis, though their own agony often pales in comparison to the horrors which they inflict on their victims. Lonely, angry, and twisted, plant husks sow their monstrous madness in the fertile corpses of wanderers who dare travel through the husk's blighted swath of wilderness. Though in their eyes any living creature is worthy of obliteration, husks reserve their most horrendous punishments for any litterer, land settler, or lumberjack who ever dared to desecrate, dominate, or denude the forest.</p>\n<h2>Monster Part Subsystem</h2>\n<p><strong>Leshy Husk Creature 0 </strong></p>\n<p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 2.25/5/9 gp</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning, piercing), armor (light), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Nature, Stealth)</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, chaotic, constitution, dexterity, energy resistant (positive), evil, mental, negative, sensory (darkvision), spells (Primal: speak with plants), strength, wild, wisdom</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary","authors":"Matt Cavanaugh","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"creatureType":""},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":1},"dex":{"mod":2},"c